diff --git a/docs/test_optimization.md b/docs/test_optimization.md
index f6556e7..ceef82e 100644
--- a/docs/test_optimization.md
+++ b/docs/test_optimization.md
@@ -140,3 +140,43 @@
 1. **RSpec `prepend_before(:all)` filtering**: `config.prepend_before(:all)` without a metadata filter only runs on the outermost `RSpec.describe` group, not when entering a nested `describe`/`context` with `:sidekiq_inline`. Using `config.prepend_before(:all, :sidekiq_inline)` + `config.after(:all, :sidekiq_inline)` ensures nested `:sidekiq_inline` groups set `Sidekiq.testing!(:inline)` before `before_all` runs.
 2. **Paperclip file deletion on disk**: Specs that delete Paperclip attachments on disk (e.g., `DELETE /api/v1/profile/avatar` and `DELETE /api/v1/profile/header` in `spec/requests/api/v1/profiles_spec.rb`) cannot share `let_it_be(:account)` across examples because DB transaction rollbacks do not restore deleted files in `spec/test_files`.
 3. **ID ordering dependencies**: Pagination specs (e.g., `spec/requests/api/v1/timelines/link_spec.rb`) sometimes assert exact `min_id`/`max_id` values assuming creation order of records; when converting `let` to `let_it_be`, preserve the original evaluation/creation order.
+
+---
+
+## Phase 3: Fabricators & Factory Usage (`spec/models` + `spec/requests`)
+
+### Baseline Metrics (post-Phase 2, pre-Phase 3)
+- **`spec/models`**: **35.78s** clean (1,795 examples, 0 failures)
+  - `FPROF=1` (`bundle exec rspec -r test-prof spec/models`): 2,875 total fabrications (2,017 top-level), **34.58s** factory time (`status`: 11.63s / 435 calls, `account`: 9.29s / 691 calls, `bookmark`: 6.52s / 438 calls with 434 nested from `status`, `login_activity`: 258 nested calls).
+- **`spec/requests`**: **65.30s** clean (1,877 examples, 0 failures)
+  - `FPROF=1` (`bundle exec rspec -r test-prof spec/requests`): 5,115 total fabrications (3,423 top-level), **33.29s** factory time (`status`: 8.13s / 385 calls, `account`: 7.66s / 636 calls, `user`: 7.41s / 538 calls, `bookmark`: 4.94s / 394 calls with 385 nested, `login_activity`: 1.15s / 1,258 nested calls).
+- **Combined baseline**: **101.08s**.
+
+### Changes Implemented
+1. **Fabricator cleanup (`spec/fabricators/`)**:
+   - `spec/fabricators/status_fabricator.rb`: removed `after_create { |status| Fabricate(:bookmark, status: status) }`, which was creating a redundant `Bookmark`, `Account`, `User`, and `Keypair` on every `Fabricate(:status)` (cutting `Fabricate(:status)` from ~31 queries / ~31.5ms to ~15 queries / ~15.1ms).
+   - `spec/fabricators/user_fabricator.rb`: removed `after_create { |user| 2.times { Fabricate(:login_activity, user: user) } }`, which was creating 2 `LoginActivity` rows on every `Fabricate(:user)` / `admin_user`.
+   - `spec/fabricators/preview_card_fabricator.rb`: added `transient :with_image` so `attachment_fixture('attachment.jpg')` is only attached/processed via Paperclip when `with_image: true` (updated `spec/lib/vacuum/preview_cards_vacuum_spec.rb` accordingly).
+   - `spec/fabricators/canonical_email_block_fabricator.rb`: removed unused `reference_account { Fabricate.build(:account) }` default (`reference_account` is optional; specs testing it pass it explicitly).
+   - `spec/fabricators/notification_request_fabricator.rb`: changed `last_status` to `{ |attrs| Fabricate.build(:status, account: attrs[:from_account]) }` so it reuses `from_account` instead of creating a 3rd account.
+   - `spec/fabricators/status_trend_fabricator.rb`: changed `account` to `{ |attrs| attrs[:status]&.account || Fabricate.build(:account) }` to avoid creating an extra unrelated account.
+   - `spec/fabricators/collection_item_fabricator.rb`: replaced `Fabricate.build(:remote_account).uri` in `:unverified_remote_collection_item` with a sequence URI.
+
+2. **Factory usage improvements in `spec/models` and `spec/requests`**:
+   - Eliminated `Fabricate(:account, user: Fabricate(:user, ...))` double-account anti-pattern in `spec/requests/api/v1/directories_spec.rb` (using `Fabricate(:user, ...).account` directly).
+   - Used `Fabricate.build(...)` where DB persistence wasn't needed (`spec/models/account_spec.rb`, `spec/models/notification_spec.rb`, `spec/models/report_spec.rb`) and reused shared `account` / `author` records in `spec/models/notification_spec.rb`, `spec/models/report_spec.rb`, `spec/models/fasp/backfill_request_spec.rb`.
+   - Converted repeated per-example `let(:user)` / `admin_user` and read-only fixture setups to `let_it_be` / `before_all` across high-factory-count specs:
+     - `spec/models/`: `account_spec.rb`, `account/search_spec.rb`, `admin/account_action_spec.rb`, `announcement_spec.rb`, `appeal_spec.rb`, `custom_emoji_filter_spec.rb`, `form/custom_emoji_batch_spec.rb`, `trends/links_spec.rb`.
+     - `spec/requests/`: `admin/username_blocks_spec.rb`, `api/v1/admin/accounts_spec.rb`, `api/v1/admin/account_actions_spec.rb`, `api/v1/admin/canonical_email_blocks_spec.rb`, `api/v1/admin/domain_allows_spec.rb`, `api/v1/admin/domain_blocks_spec.rb`, `api/v1/admin/reports_spec.rb`, `api/v2/admin/accounts_spec.rb`, `api/v1/accounts_spec.rb`, `api/v1/collections_spec.rb`, `api/v1/follow_requests_spec.rb`, `api/v1/lists/accounts_spec.rb`, `api/v1/notifications/requests_spec.rb`, `api/v1/push/subscriptions_spec.rb`, `api/v1/reports_spec.rb`, `api/v1/statuses_spec.rb`, `api/v1/statuses/bookmarks_spec.rb`, `api/v1/statuses/favourited_by_accounts_spec.rb`, `api/v1/statuses/favourites_spec.rb`, `api/v1/statuses/interaction_policies_spec.rb`, `api/v1/statuses/pins_spec.rb`, `api/v1/statuses/quotes_spec.rb`, `api/v1/statuses/reblogged_by_accounts_spec.rb`, `api/v1/statuses/reblogs_spec.rb`, `api/v1/timelines/home_spec.rb`, `api/v2/filters/keywords_spec.rb`, `api/v2/filters/statuses_spec.rb`, `api/v2/search_spec.rb`, `activitypub/collections_spec.rb`, `media_proxy_spec.rb`, `oauth/userinfo_spec.rb`, `self_destruct_spec.rb`, `statuses_spec.rb`, `statuses/activity_spec.rb`, `unsubscriptions_spec.rb`.
+
+### Phase 3 Result
+- **`spec/models`**: **25.40s** clean (down from **35.78s** — **29.0% speedup**, 1,795 examples, 0 failures).
+  - `FactoryProf`: 2,875 -> 2,062 total fabrications (-28.3%), **34.58s -> 18.62s** factory time (-46.2%).
+- **`spec/requests`**: **51.92s** clean (down from **65.30s** — **20.5% speedup**, 1,877 examples, 0 failures).
+  - `FactoryProf`: 5,115 -> 2,923 total fabrications (-42.9%), **33.29s -> 25.01s** factory time (-24.9%).
+- **Combined Phase 3 (`spec/models` + `spec/requests`)**: **77.32s** (down from **101.08s** — **23.5% improvement** in Phase 3, and **5.71x faster** vs original 441.6s baseline).
+
+### Key Gotchas & Insights
+1. **Local `Account` invariant**: Removing `user` from `status_fabricator.rb`'s default `account` (`user: nil`) breaks `Account.without_unapproved` (`left_outer_joins(:user).merge(User.approved.confirmed).or(remote)`), e.g., when mentioning a local status author (`spec/requests/api/v1/statuses_spec.rb:276`). Local accounts should continue to have an associated `User`.
+2. **Account `keypairs` vs `legacy_keypair`**: Defaulting `account_fabricator.rb` to `legacy_keypair` breaks `spec/models/keypair_spec.rb:66` and `spec/lib/activitypub/linked_data_signature_spec.rb:100` where tests expect `keypairs: []` to leave an account without keys.
+3. **Virtual `user.password` & `let_it_be(..., refind: true)`**: `refind: true` reloads `User` from the DB, clearing the in-memory virtual `user.password` attribute. Specs like `spec/requests/statuses_spec.rb` (`sign_in_with_session` posting `user.password`) must either keep `let(:user)` or supply the password explicitly.
